Entries for the Mississippi QSO Party used by in-state (Mississippi) stations
The 82 Mississippi counties (each its own multiplier), the US states with DC counted as Maryland, and the 13 Canadian provinces and territories.
DXCC countries other than the USA, Canada, Hawaii and Alaska are the class DX multiplier, not entries here; FT4/FT8 grids are its prefix multiplier.
The county file comes FIRST, so a county code wins over any state or province alias spelled the same.
DC is mapped to Md before s50.dom: the rules count 49 remaining States, and NY4I counts DC as Maryland (issue 123).
Mississippi itself is not a multiplier for an in-state entrant (the remaining States): the class refuses it.
s50.dom is included BEFORE p13.dom: p13 also spells Newfoundland LA, and the first alias added wins, so LA stays Louisiana.
NF and LB are read as NL (the last line): the rules count the 13 provinces and territories.
No line of this header may hold an equals sign: the reader takes any such line as an entry.

INCLUDE FILE mississippi_cty.dom
Dc > Md = DC
INCLUDE FILE s50.dom
INCLUDE FILE p13.dom
Nl = NF,LB
